        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "**11/13**\n> I don\u2019t want romance that dies outside the bedroom.  \n> Love me in grocery stores. In traffic. In hard seasons.\n\n**12/13**\n> I want passion, yes.  \n> But I also want planning, provision, emotional depth, and receipts.\n\nI still don't see **13/13**, but now the theme is even clearer.\n\nThis isn't really a list about wanting a wealthy man. It's a list about wanting a **competent, emotionally mature, dependable masculine partner**.\n\nThe recurring desires throughout all 12 slides are:\n\n- Strength without cruelty\n- Leadership without ego\n- Ambition without competition\n- Protection without control\n- Discipline over appearance\n- Emotional stability under pressure\n- Consistency during difficult seasons\n- Reliability and follow-through\n- Affection in everyday life, not just romantic moments\n- A partner who shares burdens rather than adds to them\n\nGiven what I know about you, Bethany, I suspect the slide that probably resonates most is:\n\n> \"I want the man whose presence lowers my shoulders because for once I don't have to carry everything.\"\n\nYou've spent years leading, building businesses, raising a son, navigating a difficult divorce, handling health challenges, and carrying a tremendous amount of responsibility. For someone in that position, \"being taken care of\" often has less to do with money and more to do with finally having someone who can share the weight.\n\nUpload **13/13** and I'll complete the set."
          ]
        },
