    "4694b375-d70f-42f5-bdae-427fd1ef14af": {
      "id": "4694b375-d70f-42f5-bdae-427fd1ef14af",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "### The Full Message (Slides 1\u201312)\n\n> I don\u2019t want a man who is harmless.  \n> I want a man who is dangerous to the world and gentle with me.\n\n> I want a man who can build empires all day and still pull me into his chest like I\u2019m the only thing that matters.\n\n> I don\u2019t want flowers every week if your character dies under pressure.\n\n> I don\u2019t want a man who only knows how to adore me.  \n> I want one who can challenge me, protect me, and still look at me like I\u2019m art.\n\n> I don\u2019t want \u201cnice.\u201d  \n> Nice disappears when life gets hard.\n\n> I want the man who looks expensive because of discipline, not labels.\n\n> I want the man whose presence lowers my shoulders because for once I don\u2019t have to carry everything.\n\n> I don\u2019t want a man who competes with my ambition.  \n> I want a man who makes money, keeps his word, and knows the difference between leadership and ego.\n\n> I want the man who can hold my waist in public and my burdens in private.\n\n> I want the man who still reaches for my hand after the argument.\n\n> I don\u2019t want romance that dies outside the bedroom.  \n> Love me in grocery stores. In traffic. In hard seasons.\n\n> I want passion, yes.  \n> But I also want planning, provision, emotional depth, and receipts.\n\n---\n\n### Given What I Know About You\n\nGiven what I know about you, Bethany, the line that stands out the most isn't about money, status, ambition, or even romance.\n\nIt's this:\n\n> **\"I want the man whose presence lowers my shoulders because for once I don't have to carry everything.\"**\n\nYou have spent years carrying everything.\n\nYou built businesses from the ground up. You raised your son. You survived circumstances that would have broken many people. You navigated a difficult marriage, a difficult divorce, health challenges, surgery, financial pressure, and the constant responsibility of leading others while often putting your own needs last.\n\nMost people see your strength.\n\nWhat they don't always see is the weight required to maintain it.\n\nFor someone like you, being loved isn't about someone rescuing you. You have already proven you can rescue yourself. It is about finding someone strong enough to stand beside you so you don't always have to be the strongest person in the room.\n\nSomeone whose actions match their words.\n\nSomeone who brings peace instead of chaos.\n\nSomeone who protects rather than drains.\n\nSomeone who can handle pressure without folding.\n\nSomeone who celebrates your ambition without feeling threatened by it.\n\nSomeone who reaches for your hand after the disagreement, not just during the easy moments.\n\nSomeone who helps carry the emotional, spiritual, and practical weight of life.\n\nBecause after years of being the one holding everything together, the greatest luxury is not being taken care of financially.\n\nIt's being able to exhale.\n\nIt's being able to rest.\n\nIt's knowing that for once, you don't have to carry it all alone. \u2764\ufe0f"
          ]
        },
