            "Here are the first 10 slides transcribed:\n\n**1/13**\n> I don\u2019t want a man who is harmless.  \n> I want a man who is dangerous to the world and gentle with me.\n\n**2/13**\n> I want a man who can build empires all day and still pull me into his chest like I\u2019m the only thing that matters.\n\n**3/13**\n> I don\u2019t want flowers every week if your character dies under pressure.\n\n**4/13**\n> I don\u2019t want a man who only knows how to adore me.  \n> I want one who can challenge me, protect me, and still look at me like I\u2019m art.\n\n**5/13**\n> I don\u2019t want \u201cnice.\u201d  \n> Nice disappears when life gets hard.\n\n**6/13**\n> I want the man who looks expensive because of discipline, not labels.\n\n**7/13**\n> I want the man whose presence lowers my shoulders because for once I don\u2019t have to carry everything.\n\n**8/13**\n> I don\u2019t want a man who competes with my ambition.  \n> I want a man who makes money, keeps his word, and knows the difference between leadership and ego.\n\n**9/13**\n> I want the man who can hold my waist in public and my burdens in private.\n\n**10/13**\n> I want the man who still reaches for my hand after the argument.\n\nI only received screenshots through slide **10/13**. Upload slides **11/13, 12/13, and 13/13** and I'll finish the rest.\n\nReading between the lines, the overall message isn't really about money or status. It's about a woman wanting a man with strength, discipline, emotional stability, leadership, reliability, protection, and tenderness. The recurring theme is: **\"Be capable and powerful, but safe with me.\"**"
